  "description": "KIZDAZ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C50 H104 Ho4 Mn5 N8 O40,2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Ho1 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Ho1A (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho2A (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Mn2A (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn3A (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.818-3.854 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 82.95-132.12°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C54H110Mn5Ho4N10O40. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 Piv (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
